    "summary": "The shutdown sequence and the fatal-error handler move from the daemon's entry point into src/daemon/shutdown.ts and src/daemon/fatal.ts; every exit goes through exitRespectingStoreHealth. With the store's health locks-lost the daemon does not wait for the queue or close the store: it removes its pid file and socket, writes one last line synchronously, and sends itself SIGKILL; the same ending replaces the exit after the drain, at the backstop and after a fatal error. closeGraphStore now probes before closing, so an unmet failure is found there. Beyond the plan's text: the SIGKILL is delayed 50 ms so the answer to the stop request leaves the socket. The real daemon entry was also started and stopped in a temporary home (clean exit, pid file and socket removed). One combined run of the daemon suites stalled in store-failure-dispatch.test.ts; it did not recur in eight repeats and the cause is not known; the tests' socket requests are now bounded.",
